 :db/id #edb/ref 17592186675715} {:answer/id #uuid "8d39481e-add9-4e48-b674-964c79953238" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2^{x}\\ln\\left(2\\right)l" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186675716} {:answer/id #uuid "c16a4364-1e3b-4318-ae93-8caeb987b96d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2^{x}\\ln\\left(2\\right)\\log_{\\placeholder{}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186675717} {:answer/id #uuid "b304f70b-b0e7-4783-8524-e20162824c8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2^{x}\\ln\\left(2\\right)\\log_7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186675718} {:answer/id #uuid "8641a99f-9992-46f0-a0ae-0f0103f4c1bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2^{x}\\ln\\left(2\\right)\\log_7\\left(\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186675719} {:answer/id #uuid "3f2fef21-1179-4abc-83a3-dabbb0323c38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2^{x} \\log_{7}(x) \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186675720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06f8e988-371d-5570-a38a-e5d41a7860f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2^{x} \\log_{7}(x) \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657610} :answer-field/id #uuid "23643de0-4f04-5b7d-97e1-51f4725c1a04" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657614}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "726b77c9-4439-577a-8549-9ccc83c65f8b" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={2}^{x}\\log _{7} (x),$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n$f^{\\prime}(x)=$\n{{field-1}} $+\\,\\frac{2^{x}}{x \\ln{\\left(7 \\right)}}$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={2}^{x}$ and $v(x)=\\log _{7} (x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & ={({2}^{x})}^{′}\\log _{7} (x)+{2}^{x}{(\\log _{7} (x))}^{′} \\\\  & =({2}^{x}\\ln  (2))(\\log _{7} (x))+({2}^{x})(\\frac{1}{x\\ln  (7)}) \\\\  & ={2}^{x}\\ln  (2)\\log _{7} (x)+\\frac{{2}^{x}}{x\\ln  (7)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186657623 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c94a4fb8-5d4b-51de-9265-fdf1204cf1e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\log_{10}(x) \\sec^{2}{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c94a4fb8-5d4b-51de-9265-fdf1204cf1e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\log_{10}(x) \\sec^{2}{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657625} :answer-field/id #uuid "66f0f5cd-b5e5-5b2f-b843-1258c616a836" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657618}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b796de74-72c4-529b-b038-a4d67224a125" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\tan(x)\\log(x),$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n**Hint:** $\\log(x)=\\log_{10}(x)$\n\n$f^{\\prime}(x)=$\n{{field-1}} $+\\,\\frac{\\tan{\\left(x \\right)}}{x \\ln{\\left(10 \\right)}}$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=\\tan(x)$ and $v(x)=\\log(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =(\\tan(x))^{′}\\log(x)+\\tan(x)(\\log(x))^{′} \\\\  & =(\\sec^{2}(x))(\\log(x))+(\\tan(x))(\\frac{1}{x\\ln(10)}) \\\\  & =\\sec^{2}(x)\\log(x)+\\frac{\\tan(x)}{x\\ln(10)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186657627 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d4fe52b-b7be-5dfe-9a62-a9bb807e825c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{3} + 4}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657620} {:answer/id #uuid "e7cb6598-216f-42c9-acbb-153b6a47e8da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^3+4}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674541}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d4fe52b-b7be-5dfe-9a62-a9bb807e825c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{3} + 4}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657620} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd8a4fb2-1b6c-5f94-bc6f-ffd7cd7945d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657631}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "dd5b6598-4397-5f58-8be5-6a17f6668cbf" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=({x}^{3}+4)\\ln(x),$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n$f^{\\prime}(x)=3 x^{2} \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\,+$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=({x}^{3}+4)$ and $v(x)=\\ln(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =(({x}^{3}+4))^{′}\\ln(x)+({x}^{3}+4)(\\ln(x))^{′} \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2})(\\ln(x))+({x}^{3}+4)(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}\\ln(x)+\\frac{{x}^{3}+4}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186659664 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fad68fff-0a85-5649-b951-8bfbebfeddbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fad68fff-0a85-5649-b951-8bfbebfeddbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659525} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d9d7154-18c6-5350-857a-26e545363d3c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659543}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "01704260-cc95-5d06-b0f7-971f614489ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-218592" :question/problem "Solve the equation $2{x}^{2}-5=1.$ Express your final answer in its simplest form.\n\n$x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the ${x}^{2}$ on one side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-5 & =1 \\\\ 2{x}^{2} & =6 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ |x| & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186659679 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "594a7ba1-0bac-51b0-9d72-c9f4f0c79094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w=\\pm 8\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659224} {:answer/id #uuid "6f61d3bc-218f-5336-9d85-35cc5655eeaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w=\\pm 4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659282} {:answer/id #uuid "a2584513-7e76-519c-ab22-96a40c75d8a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w=\\pm 4\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659375} {:answer/id #uuid "dc7701b6-f190-5df3-bd38-981eef8b9c92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w=\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659460} {:answer/id #uuid "e37dcec1-e637-51b8-ae3a-68a308d5683c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w=2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f61d3bc-218f-5336-9d85-35cc5655eeaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w=\\pm 4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659282} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a2a82b4-9b8d-5332-8b2d-c3ebd1632542" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659578}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "258ead69-099e-5710-ad15-bda6de3f681f" :question/math-academy-id "q-30211" :question/problem "Find $w$ if ${w}^{2}=48.$" :question/worked-solution "We take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{w}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{48} \\\\ |w| & =\\sqrt{16\\cdot 3} \\\\ |w| & =\\sqrt{16}\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ |w| & =4\\sqrt{3} \\\\ w & =\\pm 4\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186659687 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38bb7bba-5afd-5581-97ab-39c1c0d447da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38bb7bba-5afd-5581-97ab-39c1c0d447da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659171} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea2e2cce-c992-577d-8d63-d29c3c58b6b2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659650}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3abf8c53-a638-5d0c-9888-32ee2d2298a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-218585" :question/problem "If $4{k}^{2}-\\frac{25}{16}=0,$ then $k=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the ${k}^{2}$ on one side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{k}^{2}-\\frac{25}{16} & =0 \\\\ 4{k}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{16} \\\\ {k}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{64}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{k}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{64}} \\\\ |k| & =\\frac{\\sqrt{25}}{\\sqrt{64}} \\\\ |k| & =\\frac{5}{8} \\\\ k & =\\pm \\frac{5}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186659697 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6256e2e3-9810-55c1-a32c-94b16e16882e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659250}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6256e2e3-9810-55c1-a32c-94b16e16882e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659250} :answer-field/id #uuid "912f03c6-3884-58a2-8601-4bd5a089dbf1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659605}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "64793476-1902-50d8-8071-9a701ab217ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-218554" :question/problem "If $98-2{z}^{2}=0,$ then $z=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the ${z}^{2}$ on one side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}98-2{z}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 2{z}^{2} & =98 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =49\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{z}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ |z| & =7 \\\\ z & =\\pm 7\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186659702 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f4c5f75-4711-5e74-9a76-163f77f79189" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659090} {:answer/id #uuid "19e04381-3e8b-5719-9354-d513e7acd430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=\\pm \\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659103} {:answer/id #uuid "33a67280-a754-5e5f-9c23-5e02d63d036a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045