{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b7f0d67-a7be-5f6d-8a82-e496afd22fd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659135} {:answer/id #uuid "3eed8581-db50-5d48-ba77-d6b0726c3c24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659180} {:answer/id #uuid "7375f9f6-2d57-5de8-83be-e49ee5e30e94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659290} {:answer/id #uuid "98a26682-dad4-5fe4-9c1c-8d8fc24efc63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659353} {:answer/id #uuid "ea35b1d9-d564-5c62-9706-2bbcf93cdecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=\\pm \\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659488}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3eed8581-db50-5d48-ba77-d6b0726c3c24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659180} :answer-field/id #uuid "d44abb46-466c-5d16-8cfe-31b91d08de79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186659640}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "fcc8df11-1ca5-53f4-9bba-b2a2baf34631" :question/math-academy-id "q-30233" :question/problem "Find $n$ if $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{{n}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the ${n}^{2}$ on one side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{n}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{4} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{{n}^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{{n}^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ {n}^{2} & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{n}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}} \\\\ |n| & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}} \\\\ |n| & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ n & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186665388 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bdce6ad-b4a6-52a8-a97c-61df552de9f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}{e}^{y}+2x=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186664915} {:answer/id #uuid "30117d95-a3ce-5247-9571-29465e68f49c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1){e}^{y}+{x}^{2}=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186664956} {:answer/id #uuid "98552a50-83a8-50f5-bc6c-ce582424bf49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x+1){e}^{y}-{x}^{2}=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665097} {:answer/id #uuid "a41d28c9-7fc5-542f-81de-382d0abdc292" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1){e}^{y}+2x=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665119} {:answer/id #uuid "c5cf8173-8972-59b5-92e7-26c93e658bba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{e}^{y}+{x}^{2}=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30117d95-a3ce-5247-9571-29465e68f49c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1){e}^{y}+{x}^{2}=c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186664956} :answer-field/id #uuid "dff6e8d2-c594-54e1-b7c5-443d4db534d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "55f3d2e8-477d-5b70-816c-9bf710aff2dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-103340" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the exact differential equation\n\n$$\n({e}^{y}+2x)\\,\\text{d}x+(x+1){e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the differential equation is of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)={e}^{y}+2x$ and $Q(x,y)=(x+1){e}^{y}.$\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int ({e}^{y}+2x)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =x{e}^{y}+{x}^{2}+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int (x+1){e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =(x+1){e}^{y}+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)={x}^{2},\\,f(y)={e}^{y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n(x+1){e}^{y}+{x}^{2}=c.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186665396 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10322199-2c21-511b-844e-0160e31f85b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({y}^{4}-6x)\\,({x}^{3}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186664919} {:answer/id #uuid "52cdca53-cf94-500b-ba58-ace957f8ef0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{4}+18x+\\frac{1}{4}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186664990} {:answer/id #uuid "af9a9091-18fe-5ccf-81cb-02ea329d9a98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{4}-y+{x}^{3}{y}^{2}+18x=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665136} {:answer/id #uuid "d73036c7-bf5a-5a4c-adb7-6013b75080e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-\\frac{15}{4}{y}^{4}+18x=-\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665203} {:answer/id #uuid "e850d1d6-d9a0-55ea-9f4b-2105a110a69e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-\\frac{5}{4}{y}^{4}+18x=-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d73036c7-bf5a-5a4c-adb7-6013b75080e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-\\frac{15}{4}{y}^{4}+18x=-\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665203} :answer-field/id #uuid "886c70c3-8bde-55ad-b08d-585216b7aef4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665311}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6c77a601-9a7c-5fc8-8422-4034e12c29d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-321182" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{18+3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{15{y}^{3}-2{x}^{3}y},\n$$\n\nwith the initial condition $y(0)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by rewriting this equation in differential form.\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nStarting from \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{18+3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{15{y}^{3}-2{x}^{3}y},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe first multiply through by $(15{y}^{3}-2{x}^{3}y)\\,\\text{d}x:$\n\n$$\n(15{y}^{3}-2{x}^{3}y)\\,\\text{d}y=(18+3{x}^{2}{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we rearrange the terms:\n\n$$\n(18+3{x}^{2}{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+(2{x}^{3}y-15{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nNow, we should check for exactness. A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nFor our differential equation, we have\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=18+3{x}^{2}{y}^{2},\\,Q(x,y)=2{x}^{3}y-15{y}^{3}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\,(18+3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\,(2{x}^{3}y-15{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\\,✓\n$$\n\n \nThus, our equation is exact.\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int (18+3{x}^{2}{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =18x+{x}^{3}{y}^{2}+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int (2{x}^{3}y-15{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}{y}^{2}-\\frac{15}{4}{y}^{4}+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=18x,\\,f(y)=-\\frac{15}{4}{y}^{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-\\frac{15}{4}{y}^{4}+18x=c.\n$$\n\nThe particular solution specified by the initial condition must have $y=1$ when $x=0.$ These values determine the value of the constant $c.$ Substituting this into the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-\\frac{15}{4}{y}^{4}+18x & =c \\\\ (0)^{3}(1)^{2}-\\frac{15}{4}(1)^{4}+18\\cdot 0 & =c \\\\ c & =-\\frac{15}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-\\frac{15}{4}{y}^{4}+18x=-\\frac{15}{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186670666 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2275f5fa-bafb-572f-b6e7-d370b905f9ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/20/20e196260d4d38071108e0dbb55879348386b1eb2b502fa3b6b4423f0e367339.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670667} {:answer/id #uuid "2671a4fc-1fbc-5996-a738-9b8b5cce8b0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bf/bf2a18117030301e91784f141d5601a9971f1c6902b2ea6236f2f6b1773f53dd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670668} {:answer/id #uuid "2eda0ba7-6e23-5033-867a-c0062bad0c84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/24/24a904a600c6475d1274fa7b9e06dbed168e0ceec72c0d02b7c31dfdc3431292.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670671} {:answer/id #uuid "547596f5-e0bd-55eb-967b-d130fc7d15d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cf/cf3ae6090229f1b66486c3606840c74a07be0a37559e06bd3429dec9c458a070.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670678} {:answer/id #uuid "7762a69f-5289-5df8-bc84-20c5c2b08429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/dc/dcf4fa83568b9f4e85e4f8bf1f123b1bfc77b534ad23f452a80d12f8579fed37.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2671a4fc-1fbc-5996-a738-9b8b5cce8b0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bf/bf2a18117030301e91784f141d5601a9971f1c6902b2ea6236f2f6b1773f53dd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670668} :answer-field/id #uuid "da0ed405-0b07-554e-89ea-aa5037d1c790" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670693}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1c183240-5cb2-5523-9f74-95fbf751d6a2" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1x+(2)y?$" :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(0,1)$,$(-2,0)$,$(2,-1)$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(0,1)}=1(0)+(2)(1)=2, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,0)}=1(-2)+(2)(0)=-2, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,-1)}=1(2)+(2)(-1)=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](images/bf/bf2a18117030301e91784f141d5601a9971f1c6902b2ea6236f2f6b1773f53dd.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186670673 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26df92e3-988b-5df6-ba53-422e333c817f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f3/f3e940bbe3cf1a82d47a401fef015f4970fab7016f5e82c3bbed5b254251937b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670669} {:answer/id #uuid "2bb5f7ba-f70f-56d8-b156-55d1430c841f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1d/1dd1a2bade9c53b136f6f66e3b3affe033a51c25dee9eb800412f81ab63c68f1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670670} {:answer/id #uuid "4e721f05-03da-5b8a-ad50-2d1b49465988" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7d/7d47d65a715204c6b220483ef4373d3f7cf066812f6265f34f8b90be599fd2b0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670676} {:answer/id #uuid "b8e3ed97-bf7f-5b34-b279-c97fd94002d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9f/9f25d342472d01ef2cb83116734306cea5fc24be2788aae5527d5addae247348.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670689} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc42b79-e51c-599e-b009-ba59470c42bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f5/f51fb78a12bc37626954936b6f001ff807b97c0c55279314ec60f61ecbfde501.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dcc42b79-e51c-599e-b009-ba59470c42bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f5/f51fb78a12bc37626954936b6f001ff807b97c0c55279314ec60f61ecbfde501.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670694} :answer-field/id #uuid "68c72f0a-65e2-56fe-82e3-72824b7a97b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3cf19cc1-07eb-5993-9bf4-76492a205588" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{(-2)x+(-2)y}{4}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-2,3)$,$(-1,-1)$,$(-3,-1)$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,3)}=\\frac{(-2)(-2)+(-2)(3)}{4}=- \\frac{1}{2}, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,-1)}=\\frac{(-2)(-1)+(-2)(-1)}{4}=1, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-3,-1)}=\\frac{(-2)(-3)+(-2)(-1)}{4}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](images/f5/f51fb78a12bc37626954936b6f001ff807b97c0c55279314ec60f61ecbfde501.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186670674 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f0aa562-4688-530b-b347-e9b9102470e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e1/e1be85524cc3bf86663fead888ea9ebdcaa20f428b874158b90f00910457cbd8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670683} {:answer/id #uuid "7440c